# --- Chagas (29083573)
("29083573", "beginner", 3, "caused by the parasite Trypanosoma cruzi, first described in 1909 by Brazilian physician Carlos Chagas",
 ("Which parasite causes Chagas disease?", ["Leishmania donovani", "Plasmodium vivax", "Toxoplasma gondii", "Trypanosoma cruzi"],
  "Chagas disease (American trypanosomiasis) is caused by Trypanosoma cruzi, described by Carlos Chagas in 1909.", "Trypanosoma cruzi."),
 ("¿Qué parásito causa la enfermedad de Chagas?", ["Leishmania donovani", "Plasmodium vivax", "Toxoplasma gondii", "Trypanosoma cruzi"],
  "La enfermedad de Chagas (tripanosomiasis americana) la causa Trypanosoma cruzi, descrita por Carlos Chagas en 1909.", "Trypanosoma cruzi.")),
("29083573", "curious", 1, "transmitted primarily via contact with contaminated excrement of the reduviid bug into an open wound",
 ("How is Chagas disease mainly transmitted by the vector?", ["Through saliva injected during the bite", "Contaminated bug feces entering a wound", "By drinking water only", "By sexual contact between people"],
  "The triatomine (\"vinchuca\") defecates while feeding; parasites in feces enter through the bite wound or mucosa.", "Contaminated bug feces."),
 ("¿Cómo transmite principalmente el vector la enfermedad de Chagas?", ["Por la saliva que inyecta al picar", "Heces contaminadas en la herida", "Solo por beber agua", "Por contacto sexual entre personas"],
  "La vinchuca defeca mientras se alimenta; los parásitos de las heces entran por la herida de la picadura o mucosas.", "Heces de vinchuca.")),
("29083573", "researcher", 2, "Romana’s sign (unilateral eyelid swelling)",
 ("What is Romaña's sign in acute Chagas disease?", ["A loud heart murmur", "Bilateral swelling of both legs and feet", "One-sided painless eyelid edema", "A target-shaped skin rash"],
  "Romaña's sign is unilateral eyelid edema at a conjunctival portal of entry during acute infection.", "Unilateral eyelid swelling."),
 ("¿Qué es el signo de Romaña en el Chagas agudo?", ["Un soplo cardíaco fuerte", "Hinchazón de ambas piernas y pies", "Edema palpebral unilateral", "Un exantema en diana"],
  "El signo de Romaña es el edema palpebral unilateral en la puerta de entrada conjuntival durante la infección aguda.", "Edema palpebral unilateral.")),
("29083573", "expert", 0, "In the chronic phase, which affects approximately 30% of infected individuals, cardiac complications",
 ("What are the main complications of chronic Chagas disease?", ["Cardiomyopathy and megaviscera", "Liver cirrhosis with ascites", "Bilateral blindness", "Recurrent kidney stones"],
  "About 30% develop chronic disease: cardiomyopathy, heart failure, arrhythmias, megaesophagus or megacolon.", "Heart and megaviscera."),
 ("¿Cuáles son las principales complicaciones del Chagas crónico?", ["Miocardiopatía y megavísceras", "Cirrosis hepática con ascitis", "Ceguera bilateral", "Cálculos renales recurrentes"],
  "Cerca del 30% desarrolla enfermedad crónica: miocardiopatía, insuficiencia cardíaca, arritmias, megaesófago o megacolon.", "Corazón y megavísceras.")),

